		(property "Note" "Both DIR tied to VCCA (+2V5) = A->B, both OE* tied low - ALWAYS enabled. These four channels sit on nets that this board's own 3.3 V -> 2.5 V translators drive when the HL2 pin is an input; a translator A-side input is a ~5 pF load and never a driver, so that is not contention. What decides whether an auxiliary signal reaches the cable is the LVDS driver's EN, not this part."
			(at 762 54.61 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Description" "4-bit dual-supply level translator, VCCA 2.5 V / VCCB 3.3 V. The AUX group: all four auxiliary pins on their way to the LVDS driver inputs, with G1 clock and data in port 1 and G2 clock and data in port 2"
			(at 762 54.61 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
