		(property "Note" "EN tied high, EN* tied low: ALWAYS enabled, in both roles. That is deliberate and it is safe. A receiver input is high impedance, so listening to a pair this board is also driving costs nothing; the outputs for the driven group simply go to a translator port that is disabled, so they reach no HL2 pin."
			(at 172.72 139.7 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Description" "Quad LVDS receiver, 400 Mbps, TSSOP-16. Sits across ALL FOUR AUX pairs in both roles - the two it receives and the two its own drivers drive"
